Feature: TC_12_STAFF - Scheme Selection BISS CRISS Protein Eco MSSM RCSM Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for Scheme Selection - Add BISS, CRISS" (BISSAGL-5919, AT-TC-01 to 04,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14880 / 14879 / 14877 / 14876)
  #           "Regression Pack for Scheme Selection - Add MSSM, RCSM" (BISSAGL-7582, AT-TC-01 to 05,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14893 / 14889 / 14885 / 14891 / 14890)
  # Rewritten 15-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary. Modernised 21-10-2026: the repeated journeys are merged, so each
  # check runs once. Three scenarios, so a failing card check does not stop the submit check and the report shows which
  # part broke.
  #
  # Scenario 01 - Cards and abandoned selections (nothing is submitted)          BISSAGL-14880, 14877, 14893
  #   - BISS and CRISS cards: position, acronym, full name, View Details dialog, toggle
  #   - CRISS and Protein Aid Scheme selected, Next, Back, deselected: the application is as it was
  #   - MSSM and RCSM cards (2024): acronym and full name; selected and deselected: as they were
  # Scenario 02 - One amendment changes CRISS, Protein Aid Scheme and Eco        BISSAGL-14879, 14891, 14890
  #   - submitted, recorded in the history today, all three flipped; reset in one submit, all three back
  # Scenario 03 - Other herds report a selection state                           BISSAGL-14889, 14885, 14876
  #   - A1211644 and P1461522: MSSM and RCSM report a state (legacy only opened them - "Need MSSM and RCSM disabled herd")
  #   - inactive herd N1041714: all ten schemes report a state
  #
  # What was merged (legacy -> here):
  #   - Select-then-deselect was done three times (CRISS, Protein with Next / Back, MSSM / RCSM). It is now one CRISS +
  #     Protein Aid Scheme pass through Next / Back, and one MSSM / RCSM pass on 2024, where those cards are shown.
  #     The selection is now checked as flipped after the click, before it is undone (legacy never checked it).
  #   - Change, submit, check and reset was done twice (CRISS + Protein, then Eco; BISSAGL-7582 AT-TC-04 and 05 were the
  #     same clicks). It is now one amendment with all three schemes and one reset: 2 submits instead of 4.
  #   - "the selection state should be readable" on J1400098 is covered by "notes the selection state" (it fails when a
  #     card shows no state), so it is not repeated before a change.
  #   - The amendment of J1400098 2026 is opened 3 times instead of 7.
  #   - The MSSM / RCSM card text uses the same card table as BISS / CRISS (blank position = found by acronym).
  #
  # Protein Aid Scheme: when Submit Changes reports that the Protein Scheme has no eligible crop, the submit step clicks
  # OK, gives the first tillage parcel the crop staff.protein.crop (Beans - Spring) and submits again; the reset submit
  # puts that parcel's old Parcel Use back first (StaffSteps 21-10-2026).
  #
  # Test data (kept as literals, as in legacy):
  #   J1400098 / 2026 (amended and reset; left as it was found) and J1400098 / 2024 (MSSM / RCSM cards),
  #   A1211644 / 2024, P1461522 / 2024, N1041714 / 2024 (inactive).
  #   Login agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (Scheme selection and amendments, History)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

